    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Matt Chapman** (69.85) stands as our clear anchor, benefiting from a prime leadoff spot against the shaky E-Rod and an elite BvP track record that warrants an aggressive start despite the platoon disadvantage. Similarly, **Dylan Beavers** (65.54) and **Geraldo Perdomo** (62.85) provide excellent floor-to-ceiling potential. **Beavers** capitalizes on a favorable park factor and a manageable matchup against Burke, while **Perdomo**\u2019s promotion to the number two hole, combined with his elite sprint speed profile, makes him a priority play to bolster our scarcest category, SB.\n\n**Cal Raleigh** (58.10) and **Luis Arraez** (59.42) sit right on the cusp of our \"Strong\" threshold. While **Arraez** lacks the power upside, his placement in the two-hole against a subpar starter provides the necessary volume to justify his inclusion over less favorable middle-infield options. The most difficult decision rested on the bench, where **Brendan Donovan** narrowly missed the final utility cut. While **Donovan** offers high-contact reliability, the optimizer preferred the raw park-adjusted upside of **Beavers** and the speed-heavy profile of **Perdomo**, leaving **Donovan** as our primary pivot should any late-inning defensive replacements or unexpected scratches occur.\n\nWe remain cautious regarding the weather and lineup volatility for the late games. With **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Will Smith**, **Daulton Varsho**, and **Tyler Freeman** currently unavailable, our depth is being tested, though we are confident that the tactical placement of **Taylor Ward** and **Lawrence Butler** in the OF provides the right balance of run-scoring potential and speed. We will be monitoring the status of **Masyn Winn** and **Jung Hoo Lee** closely throughout the afternoon; their absence from today's primary configuration is purely a result of the efficiency-first cap management strategy, but they remain ready for high-leverage pinch hitting duties if needed.",
